00:07:28,973 --> 00:07:31,655
[SPEAKER_01]: ...that you're really, really wound up by... Yeah.

128
00:07:33,188 --> 00:07:42,252
[SPEAKER_01]: If you keep observing that, you will remain ignorant of the nature of seeing, because you're fully absorbed with the object of your sight, which is what the sight is.

129
00:07:42,972 --> 00:07:52,115
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is, you understand the arising and ceasing, whatever you want to call it, of the eye, which is a necessary basis for any type of sight, pleasing or displeasing.

130
00:07:52,496 --> 00:07:54,697
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can't see the eye on the level of sight.

131
00:07:56,323 --> 00:08:03,009
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you get to see the truth of the I, but not by the physical, actual seeing, because that's secondary thing.

132
00:08:04,771 --> 00:08:08,134
[SPEAKER_00]: But, back onto that Pali... That's right.

133
00:08:08,254 --> 00:08:11,937
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that Buddha, Bodhisattva Vipassi,

134
00:08:12,855 --> 00:08:14,096
[SPEAKER_00]: When he talks about rise and fall...

135
