00:31:56,605 --> 00:31:58,487
[SPEAKER_01]: It wasn't a random man had the wrong view.

595
00:31:59,687 --> 00:32:03,550
[SPEAKER_01]: And I was like, yeah, no, that's probably because there's the real nibbāna, you know, the mystical experience of nibbāna.

596
00:32:03,850 --> 00:32:04,231
[SPEAKER_01]: And then this

597
00:32:07,193 --> 00:32:15,962
[SPEAKER_01]: And I was quite surprised they were saying that, because in the same sutta, the Buddha continues, and says, this man is describing nibbāna.

598
00:32:16,883 --> 00:32:22,208
[SPEAKER_01]: The man who says, I am nibbāna, nibbāna is mine, he factually asserts that which nibbāna is.

599
00:32:23,609 --> 00:32:25,691
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I read that out loud, and it was just silence.

600
00:32:26,412 --> 00:32:28,454
[SPEAKER_00]: Just... No.

601
00:32:29,395 --> 00:32:31,177
[SPEAKER_01]: So, and that's the perfect example

602
00:32:32,096 --> 00:32:34,757
[SPEAKER_01]: of that completely limited, wrong context.

603
00:32:34,777 --> 00:32:34,997
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

604
00:32:35,157 --> 00:32:40,119
[SPEAKER_01]: You have an idea of what nibbāna is, and here you are in the same... from the same person, the Buddha himself.

605
00:32:40,739 --> 00:32:46,742
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, no, that man also describes nibbāna, and that doesn't fit with your... nibbāna is indescribable.

606
00:32:46,782 --> 00:32:46,962
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

607
00:32:48,002 --> 00:32:55,245
[SPEAKER_01]: But the Buddha said, this man, with the wrong view, describes that which nibbāna is, but he doesn't attain it, because he still prioritizes his sense of self.

608
00:32:57,321 --> 00:32:58,622
[SPEAKER_01]: And you couldn't make sense out of it.

609
00:32:58,762 --> 00:32:59,682
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you have two options.

610
00:33:00,143 --> 00:33:02,484
[SPEAKER_01]: Either you ignore that you just contradicted the Buddha.

611
00:33:03,344 --> 00:33:03,545
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

612
00:33:04,525 --> 00:33:06,406
[SPEAKER_01]: Or you realize that you must... And hold on to your own view.

613
00:33:06,506 --> 00:33:06,926
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

614
00:33:07,087 --> 00:33:08,587
[SPEAKER_01]: Automatically, that's what it's implied.

615
00:33:08,707 --> 00:33:11,449
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is why you would choose to contradict or pretend you didn't hear it.

616
00:33:11,669 --> 00:33:11,809
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

617
00:33:12,570 --> 00:33:12,990
[SPEAKER_01]: It was like a...

618
00:33:13,850 --> 00:33:17,092
[SPEAKER_01]: When I read it out loud, it was just like a... You could hear, you know, the tumbleweed.

619
00:33:17,292 --> 00:33:18,013
[SPEAKER_01]: The silence.

620
00:33:19,869 --> 00:33:24,252
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, anyway, in discussion, just like... like it never happened.

621
00:33:24,733 --> 00:33:25,834
[SPEAKER_01]: Like it never happened.

622
00:33:26,714 --> 00:33:29,857
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, alternatively, you realize, oh, no, that I cannot tolerate that.

623
00:33:30,017 --> 00:33:31,978
[SPEAKER_01]: I should not tolerate that contradiction.

624
00:33:33,560 --> 00:33:40,625
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I must now undo the context of what I thought nibbāna and my goal and my 20 years of practice were leading to, and upgrade it.

625
00:33:41,706 --> 00:33:46,610
[SPEAKER_01]: That we'll be able to include this, which means I need to clarify even what I thought I understood, which I haven't.

626
00:33:47,693 --> 00:33:50,634
[SPEAKER_01]: Not protect it blindly against anything that might challenge it.

627
00:33:50,714 --> 00:33:55,577
[SPEAKER_01]: And it goes the same, by the way, in Mūlaparāyāsutta.

628
00:33:55,777 --> 00:33:56,217
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

629
00:33:56,237 --> 00:33:57,358
[SPEAKER_00]: Conceive the nibbāna.

630
00:33:57,438 --> 00:33:58,398
[SPEAKER_01]: Conceives in nibbāna.

631
00:33:58,438 --> 00:33:58,978
[SPEAKER_00]: Takes nibbāna.

632
00:33:59,059 --> 00:34:00,759
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, there must be... No, it's a real nibbāna.

633
00:34:01,280 --> 00:34:02,460
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a real nibbāna, exactly.

634
00:34:03,721 --> 00:34:10,824
[SPEAKER_01]: So, by all means, conceive nibbāna as yours, means you've done much more work than if you just conceive centrality as yours.

635
00:34:11,525 --> 00:34:13,806
[SPEAKER_01]: But fundamentally, yes, conceiving is still there.

636
00:34:14,486 --> 00:34:16,107
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means the wrong order is still there.

637
00:34:16,765 --> 00:34:20,188
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means what this man understood, the right order, hasn't been understood.

638
00:34:20,628 --> 00:34:24,511
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's like the example of how can somebody become enlightened almost in an instant.

639
00:34:24,571 --> 00:34:33,959
[SPEAKER_01]: It's because they've done all the work of replacing any inferior conceiving with the conceiving of nibbāna, conceiving of dispassion, disenchantment, letting go.

640
00:34:35,360 --> 00:34:43,067
[SPEAKER_01]: And imagine, you've done all that work already, and all you need to do now is see that as first, and your sense of self as second.

641
00:34:43,147 --> 00:34:43,507
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

642
00:34:43,587 --> 00:34:44,448
[SPEAKER_01]: That's all that's left.

643
00:34:45,534 --> 00:34:47,976
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you realize, oh no, that's why they became arahants.

644
00:34:48,196 --> 00:34:51,398
[SPEAKER_01]: Just the Buddha said one sentence, minds were enlightened.

645
00:34:51,638 --> 00:34:56,621
[SPEAKER_01]: Because they've done all the work of fixing the right order and now just understanding it as such.

646
00:34:57,642 --> 00:34:59,643
[SPEAKER_01]: And again, as we mentioned before, the bhagya sutta.

647
00:35:00,604 --> 00:35:04,947
[SPEAKER_01]: People think he was just lucky that the Buddha told him that in the scene there'll just be the scene.

648
00:35:05,947 --> 00:35:12,912
[SPEAKER_01]: And they ignore the fact that he was a quite austere, bark-wearing ascetic for who knows how long, decades maybe.

649
00:35:14,200 --> 00:35:20,123
[SPEAKER_00]: Of extreme renunciation and commitment, and he genuinely thought he was enlightened, because there's absolutely pure, perfect dispassion.

650
00:35:20,203 --> 00:35:22,504
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing, nothing can affect him.

651
00:35:25,725 --> 00:35:27,906
[SPEAKER_01]: And when he heard the Buddha, he thought, oh, okay, that was the missing bit.

652
00:35:28,426 --> 00:35:28,787
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

653
00:35:29,747 --> 00:35:32,008
[SPEAKER_01]: All he, all he needed was utterance of another.

654
00:35:32,328 --> 00:35:34,569
[SPEAKER_01]: He already developed yoniso, manasikāra thoroughly.

655
00:35:35,970 --> 00:35:36,150
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

656
00:35:37,610 --> 00:35:38,991
[SPEAKER_01]: The two factors for the right view.

657
00:35:39,591 --> 00:35:42,933
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he hadn't... he hadn't thought to change the order.

658
00:35:43,734 --> 00:35:46,856
[SPEAKER_01]: And you cannot think that without external instruction.

659
00:35:47,256 --> 00:35:49,337
[SPEAKER_01]: If you do, you will be samasambuddha.

660
00:35:49,417 --> 00:35:54,160
[SPEAKER_00]: But he had done the work in discerning the phenomena.

661
00:35:54,520 --> 00:35:55,080
[SPEAKER_00]: Absolutely.

662
00:35:55,180 --> 00:35:56,521
[SPEAKER_01]: Absolutely.

663
00:35:56,541 --> 00:36:02,965
[SPEAKER_01]: The mind, the sun, the nature, passion, the value of this passion, the restraint, all of that.

664
00:36:03,065 --> 00:36:04,386
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that he has fully understood.

665
00:36:07,074 --> 00:36:10,857
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what we meant by some beings would have little dust in their eyes.

666
00:36:11,177 --> 00:36:19,963
[SPEAKER_01]: It means the pollutions have been either undone or haven't been developed or the effort has been made and, you know, they've been abandoned.

667
00:36:20,404 --> 00:36:31,232
[SPEAKER_01]: Like his previous teachers that he wanted to go and teach, not out of gratitude or some devotional respect, but simply because it's the least work for him.

668
00:36:32,252 --> 00:36:33,573
[SPEAKER_01]: You say, oh, who should I teach first?

669
00:36:33,633 --> 00:36:36,095
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, there are those beings that need very little teaching.

670
00:36:36,195 --> 00:36:37,216
[SPEAKER_01]: Why don't I start with them?

671
00:36:53,469 --> 00:36:56,912
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, so, yeah, the Buddha just ends that sutta.

672
00:36:56,932 --> 00:36:58,894
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, he then goes through and talks about

673
00:36:59,910 --> 00:37:03,195
[SPEAKER_00]: The various factors of awakening have been obtained by him.

674
00:37:05,047 --> 00:37:07,688
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why I think it's... what he's saying is, look, isn't it amazing?

675
00:37:07,708 --> 00:37:09,669
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how much has been done by me?

676
00:37:09,809 --> 00:37:14,891
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, it's... people might think that sounds conceited, but it's just fact.

677
00:37:14,911 --> 00:37:17,512
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, to put it in, it sounds conceited, but it's just a factual statement.

678
00:37:17,532 --> 00:37:17,912
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

679
00:37:17,992 --> 00:37:19,972
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not... this is not based on conceit.

680
00:37:20,012 --> 00:37:21,253
[SPEAKER_00]: It's talking about the lack of conceit.

681
00:37:21,273 --> 00:37:23,374
[SPEAKER_01]: It's based on abandonment of the conceit.

682
00:37:23,434 --> 00:37:24,774
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's... that's why it's so amazing.

683
00:37:25,634 --> 00:37:28,696
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's... and so the sutta just ends with the Buddha saying... You know, whenever

684
00:37:32,977 --> 00:37:36,799
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, I can glide the sun and fly in the sky and things like that.

685
00:37:37,779 --> 00:37:39,180
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, that's extremely conceited, isn't it?

686
00:37:39,200 --> 00:37:40,261
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

687
00:37:40,781 --> 00:37:41,641
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just factual.

688
00:37:41,701 --> 00:37:42,022
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

689
00:37:42,302 --> 00:37:43,562
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I can and it is amazing.

690
00:37:44,623 --> 00:37:46,224
[SPEAKER_01]: You're amazed by yourself.

691
00:37:46,264 --> 00:37:46,564
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, wow.

692
00:37:46,584 --> 00:37:47,444
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah, exactly.

693
00:37:47,544 --> 00:37:49,185
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's not based on your conceit.

694
00:37:49,245 --> 00:37:50,226
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not based on I am.

695
00:37:53,227 --> 00:37:56,329
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, and then the Buddha responds and says, good, good, Udayi.

696
00:37:56,429 --> 00:37:58,930
[SPEAKER_00]: This path, Udayi, has indeed been obtained by you.

697
00:38:00,207 --> 00:38:11,118
[SPEAKER_00]: Which, when developed by you, made much of, dwelling in this way, will bring you to the truth, so that you will understand birth is destroyed, whole life has been lived, what should be done has been done, there is no more of this.

698
00:38:14,802 --> 00:38:15,062
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

